* LM324_SIMPLE.lib - simplified quad LM324 behavioral model for ngspice/KiCad
* 14-pin physical DIP/SOIC pin order. Self-contained; no external dependencies.
* Approximate characteristics: open-loop gain 100,000 V/V; GBW ~1 MHz;
* output low limit VEE+0.02 V, high limit VCC-1.5 V (light load).
* Input resistance approximated; output resistance 50 ohm.
* NOT modeled: accurate slew-rate limiting, input offset/bias currents,
* common-mode range, noise, overload recovery, supply current or loading effects.
* Use for initial simulation and check results against real hardware.
*
* KiCad model: device SUBCKT, name LM324_SIMPLE, this library file.
* Symbol pin map: 1=P1 2=P2 3=P3 4=P4 5=P5 6=P6 7=P7
*                 8=P8 9=P9 10=P10 11=P11 12=P12 13=P13 14=P14
* 4 = VCC (+9 V), 11 = VEE (0 V).
*
.SUBCKT LM324_SIMPLE P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 P7 P8 P9 P10 P11 P12 P13 P14
XA P3  P2  P4 P11 P1  LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL
XB P5  P6  P4 P11 P7  LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL
XC P10 P9  P4 P11 P8  LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL
XD P12 P13 P4 P11 P14 LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL
.ENDS LM324_SIMPLE

* One dominant-pole, voltage-output amplifier.
* A0=100k, fp~10 Hz, GBW~1 MHz.
.SUBCKT LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL INP INM VCC VEE OUT
RIN INP INM 10MEG
RINP INP VEE 100MEG
RINM INM VEE 100MEG
EGAIN NGAIN VEE INP INM 100000
RP NGAIN NFILT 100K
CP NFILT VEE 159.15N
* Clipping tracks the supply rails; output high swing is approximate.
BCLIP NDRIVE VEE V={max(0.02,min(V(VCC,VEE)-1.5,V(NFILT,VEE)))}
ROUT NDRIVE OUT 50
.ENDS LM324_SIMPLE_CHANNEL
